  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-zgit",
      "text": "English | [中文](./README.zh.md)\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-zgit)\n[](./LICENSE)"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-zgit",
      "text": "> [!TIP]\n> **第一个《世界计划》本地化知识库，为同人作者和考据党而生：[SekaiSync](https://github.com/omoinoki/sekaisync)**  \n> **The first *Project SEKAI* localization knowledge base, built for fan creators and lore enthusiasts: [SekaiSync](https://github.com/omoinoki/sekaisync)**\n>\n> 即将面向 DeepSeek Harness 插件生态针对性适配，欢迎各位豆腐人 Star 和共建。  \n> Targeted adaptation for the DeepSeek Harness plugin ecosystem is coming soon. Fellow Tofus are welcome to star and contribute!"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-zgit",
      "text": "**dsh-zgit** (the `/zgit` plugin) is a [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (dsh) plugin for when the first thought about fetching source code or binary releases from a git host should *not* be `git clone`.\n\nIt fetches over plain HTTPS, with **no git binary** and **zero runtime dependencies**:\n\n**Docs:** https://zukunftsholz.github.io/dsh-zgit/"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-zgit",
      "text": "- **Source code** → downloaded as a forge archive (codeload-style tar.gz/zip), extracted into a **simulated checkout** with `.zerogit` metadata — a git-like directory you can inspect, `status`-check, and refresh.\n- **Binary releases** → release assets listed or downloaded straight from GitHub/GitLab/Gitee releases, with sha256 verification against shipped checksum files.\n- **git, simulated** → `zgit_ls_remote`, `zgit_show`, `zgit_ls_tree`, `zgit_log`, `zgit_diff`, `zgit_status` reimplement the read side of git over the forge APIs.\n- **Anything else** → `zgit_download` fetches any direct URL (mirrors, toolchains) into the workspace with a byte cap and optional sha256."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-zgit",
      "text": "```\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-zgit"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-zgit",
      "text": "```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | git analog | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `zgit_ls_remote` | `git ls-remote` | Branches, tags, ref→sha resolution, default branch, latest release tag. |\n| `zgit_clone` | `git clone` / `git archive` | Downloads the source archive at a ref, extracts it into the workspace as a simulated checkout (`.zerogit/meta.json`), supports `subdir` sparse extraction and explicit archive URLs (mirrors). |\n| `zgit_fetch_release` | `gh release download` | Lists or downloads release assets (latest or a tag) with glob patterns and sha256 verification. |\n| `zgit_show` | `git show` | Fetches one raw file at a ref (optionally saved into the workspace). |\n| `zgit_ls_tree` | `git ls-tree` | Lists files/dirs at a ref via the forge API. |\n| `zgit_log` | `git log` | Recent commits at a ref. |\n| `zgit_diff` | `git diff` | Compare two refs: changed-files summary or a single-file unified diff. |\n| `zgit_status` | `git status` + `git fetch` | Checks a simulated checkout against the remote: moved ref, commits behind. |\n| `zgit_download` | `curl` | Any direct HTTPS download into the workspace, capped, with optional sha256. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "Plus the human-plane command **`/zgit`** (Web UI slash menu / TUI): `clone`, `get`, `show`, `ls`, `log`, `diff`, `resolve`, `status`, `download` — the same operations without the model in the loop."
    },
    {
      "section": "Forge support",
      "text": "- **GitHub** (`github.com` + `api.github.com` + `codeload.github.com` + `raw.githubusercontent.com`)\n- **GitLab** (`gitlab.com` + API v4), including nested groups\n- **Gitee** (`gitee.com` + API v5)\n- **Generic** GitHub-style hosts: archive/raw URL guessing works (self-hosted Gitea/GitHub Enterprise); API-backed operations report a clear error — use `archiveUrl` or `zgit_download`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Forge support",
      "text": "Repo references accept `owner/repo`, `owner/repo@ref`, full `https://` URLs (with `@ref` or `/tree/ref`), `git@host:owner/repo.git`, and `ssh://` URLs."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "All config lives in the plugin row (`$DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml`, the profile patch, or an overlay):\n\n```yaml\n- id: zgit\n  config:\n    clone: true          # per-tool toggles: lsRemote, clone, release, show,\n    command: true        #   lsTree, log, diff, status, download, command\n\nTokens raise API rate limits and enable private repos; the env-var name wins over a direct value."
    },
    {
      "section": "The simulated checkout",
      "text": "`zgit_clone` produces a normal directory plus:\n\n```\n<dir>/\n├── .zerogit/\n│   ├── meta.json   # origin, ref, sha, archive URL, fetched-at, file counts\n│   └── HEAD        # the pinned commit sha\n\n`zgit_status <dir>` re-resolves the pinned ref remotely and reports how far the checkout fell behind. Refresh with `zgit_clone (replace: true)`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Safety properties",
      "text": "- **Workspace confinement** — every write is resolved inside the calling session's workspace (`exec.agent.session.header.cwd`), falling back to `workspaceRoot` for agentless callers; paths escaping the root are rejected.\n- **Archive hardening** — path traversal (`..`, absolute paths, Windows reserved names) is rejected; case-insensitive collisions error; entries are capped by count and total bytes; zip entries are CRC32-verified; gzip is decompressed under a hard cap (bomb guard); symlinks are recorded and skipped (not materialized), hardlinks are copied.\n- **Byte caps** everywhere — downloads stream with early abort when a cap is exceeded.\n- **No execution** — archives are never executed, only extracted."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "The package has **zero runtime dependencies** (pure Node builtins: `node:zlib`, `node:crypto`, `node:fs`, `node:http`). It targets DSH **0.1.7-rc.2** (cordis 4.0.4, schemastery 3.18.4) and also supports 0.1.5-rc.2. Tests run against the project's own pinned `@deepseek-ai/*` devDependencies — the versions this package declares and CI installs:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm run build      # scripts/build.sh (DSH checkout + junctions + tsc) via node wrapper\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm test           # vitest: parser/glob units, tar.gz+zip extractors, forge fixtures, real-HTTP e2e, Cordis mount\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "FAQ",
      "text": "**What is dsh-zgit?**\ndsh-zgit (zgit) is a DeepSeek Harness plugin that fetches source archives and release assets from git hosts over plain HTTPS. It needs no git binary and adds no runtime dependencies.\n\n**Do I need git installed?**\nNo. Everything runs over HTTPS against the forge's archive, raw-file, and release endpoints."
    },
    {
      "section": "FAQ",
      "text": "**Which git hosts are supported?**\nGitHub, GitLab (API v4, nested groups), and Gitee (API v5). Generic GitHub-style self-hosted hosts (Gitea, GitHub Enterprise) work for archive/raw URL guessing; API-backed operations return a clear error and fall back to `archiveUrl` or `zgit_download`.\n\n**How do I install it?**\n`dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-zgit` — the package is on npm. The Git form (`github:zukunftsholz/dsh-zgit`) and a local checkout (`./dsh-zgit`) work too."
    },
    {
      "section": "FAQ",
      "text": "**Is it a git replacement?**\nIt reimplements the read side of git (`ls-remote`, `show`, `ls-tree`, `log`, `diff`, `status`) over the forge APIs, plus release-asset download. It does not do writes or pushes.\n\n**Are downloads verified?**\nRelease assets and `zgit_download` support sha256 verification against shipped checksum files. Zip entries are CRC32-verified; gzip is decompressed under a hard cap (bomb guard)."
    },
    {
      "section": "FAQ",
      "text": "**Which DSH version does it target?**\nDSH 0.1.7-rc.2 (cordis 4.0.4, schemastery 3.18.4); 0.1.5-rc.2 remains supported.\n\n**What license?**\nMIT."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
